 "description": "One request: a base64 image of 250,000 bytes (1,000 tokens at 1 token for 250 bytes) beside text. The client body holds 1,000 + 2,000 text tokens and the image: 4,000 tokens. The operator cuts m2 from 2,000 to 500 tokens. The forwarded body is billed 1,000 + 1,000 + 500 = 2,500 tokens. The text ratio leaves the image out: (2,500 - 1,000) tokens over (4,000 + 2,000) forwarded text bytes = 1,500 / 6,000 = 0.25 tokens a byte. The cut removes 6,000 bytes: 6,000 x 0.25 = 1,500 tokens saved, at the cache write tier. If the image were counted in the ratio, 250,000 extra bytes would drag the ratio to 0.0098 and the saving to 59 tokens.",
